{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>מכשפה</b> — letters of המכשף (the sorcerer); one alef for the man and one alef for the woman, except that Scripture speaks of that which is commonplace. And juxtaposed to it: כל שוכב עם בהמה — most forbidden relations come about through sorcery. Another interpretation: an allusion to Balaam the soothsayer, who lay with his she-ass. ס\"ת כל שוכב and the word עם — letters of בלעם. And juxtaposed to it: זובח לאלהים יחרם — most sorcery comes about through slaughter to idolatry:" "<b>לא תחיה</b> — three times in the Masorah: this one, and the other two: לא תחיה כל נשמה; החכמה תחיה בעליה. In the Midrash: the Amalekites were sorcerers and would make themselves in the likeness of animals to escape, therefore HaShem commanded: והמתה מאיש עד אשה מעולל ועד יונק משור ועד שה וגו', and this is because of the wisdom that was in them, and they sought to keep themselves alive through their wisdom, so Scripture commanded: לא תחיה כל נשמה, and: מכשפה לא תחיה:"], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "In the notarikon, עם (the word 'with' in כל שוכב עם בהמה) is read as letters א-מ, which together with the remaining letters of כל שוכב rearrange to בלעם."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:06.475521366Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}